# Session Restart Notes (~/proj)

_Cross-repo notes. Repo-specific knowledge lives in each repo (CLAUDE.md,
uvm/vlt/README.md). Updated periodically by Claude._

Last updated: 2026-08-27

## UVM-on-Verilator CAMPAIGN — HONEST STATUS (2026-08-27)

Goal: give every license-gated UVM bench a license-free OSS Verilator build+run
in cloud CI (GitHub Actions builds Verilator 5.050 from source, lint + smoke).

### IMPORTANT CORRECTION
CI reported "success" on EXIT CODE only. The UVM sim exits 0 even with
UVM_ERRORs, so "success" did NOT mean the smoke test passed. Real status below.

### What is genuinely done
- Flow + CI added to 8 repos; benches now BUILD and RUN under Verilator 5.050 in
  the cloud (was impossible without VCS/Xcelium).
- Verilator (first tool to ever parse these never-licensed benches) caught real
  latent bugs, fixed:
  * cxl_lpddr5x: task closed with endfunction -> endtask.
  * chi-to-ucie: mailbox put() (blocking task) called in a function -> try_put().
  * axi4_to_dfi_ddr: `uvm_field_time (not a UVM macro) -> `uvm_field_int;
    illegal bit-select on paren-expr -> sized cast ID_W'(...).
- si5_prep: private repo created + pushed (was LOCAL-ONLY). Verilator PORT
  DEFERRED: reserved-word identifiers used as names (checker, strong),
  import "DPI-C" inside a class, $get_coverage — needs refactor/guards.

### ROOT CAUSE FOUND + FIXED (2026-08-27): z3 solver missing in CI
Verilator solves randomize() constraints via an external SMT solver (z3/cvc5)
at RUNTIME. GitHub runners have none -> every constrained randomize() returns 0
-> mass UVM_ERRORs. Local works because z3/cvc5 are on PATH (~/oss-cad-suite/bin).
FIX = `apt-get install -y z3` in each verilator-uvm.yml (next to ccache). Proven:
probe 0/10 -> 10/10; apb-to-mem-all-py smoke 64 errors -> 0/0. Also added
timeout-minutes: 30 to guard runaway hangs (axi4_dfi had hung ~3h). z3+timeout
pushed to all 8 repos; re-running. See memory [[oss-uvm-verilator]].

### (historical) THE BLOCKER (true-pass): randomize() fails under UVM on Verilator
Real UVM results (build+run OK, but tests do not pass):
| repo | UVM_ERROR | UVM_FATAL |
|------|-----------|-----------|
| apb-to-mem-all-py | 64 | 0 |
| uvm_review | 64 | 0 |
| apb-to-mem-bazel | 64 | 0 |
| cxl_lpddr5x_bridge | 32 | 0 |
| ucie-cxl-bridge | 0 | 1 (FATAL) |
| axi-on-ucie / chi-to-ucie / axi4_dfi | (runs were still completing) | |
Dominant cause = `apb_seq_item randomize() failed` on every txn. Verified:
randomize() with inline constraints WORKS standalone in Verilator 5.050 (minimal
test ok=10 fail=0), but FAILS on uvm_sequence_item-derived classes (through the
UVM base-class chain). This is a Verilator/UVM randomize maturity issue, not a
testbench bug — needs dedicated investigation, not a quick edit.

### Decision needed from user (asked 2026-08-27)
How to treat UVM_ERRORs / gate policy, and whether to invest in the
Verilator-UVM randomize fix for true passes vs. ship build+run+no-FATAL CI and
document the errors. Remaining repos not yet done: 3 small
(IP-ucie-rdi-to-pcie-pipe, chi-to-bow-bridge, ucie_rdi_to_pcie6_pipe7) + si5_prep
port. Ledger: scratchpad/campaign_ledger.md.

## General WSL2 RAM ceiling / OSS Verilator toolchain
- Host ~8 GB (WSL sees ~5.7 GB); memory=16GB in .wslconfig is ignored. Verilator
  --lint-only ~330 MB (safe); full --binary OOMs -> build in cloud CI.
- ~/verilator/bin/verilator = 5.050 (only local UVM-capable one). unset
  VERILATOR_ROOT after sourcing OSS CAD Suite env. UVM_HOME=
  ~/verilator/test_regress/t/uvm. See memory [[oss-uvm-verilator]].
- SSH origin fails here; push via HTTPS (gh logged in as markrthomas).
